{{- /*
  IKEA IDÅSEN desk - https://newam.github.io/idasen/index.html#configuration

  The address is per-host, not per-desk: macOS never exposes BLE MACs, so
  CoreBluetooth hands out an opaque UUID derived from this specific Mac. The
  same desk therefore has a different address on every machine. Linux reports
  the real MAC and would be portable.

  Adding a new machine - scan for it, then add a line to the dict below:
    uvx --with bleak python -c 'import asyncio, bleak; print(asyncio.run(bleak.BleakScanner.discover(timeout=10)))'
  Unlisted hosts fall through to the placeholder that `idasen init` writes,
  so the file is inert rather than broken until it is filled in.

  Note: the desk's Linak controller accepts one BLE connection at a time - the
  phone's Desk Control app will lock the CLI out while it is connected.
*/ -}}
{{- $deskAddress := get (dict
      "Bishop" "F0700AEC-8D8F-2DAF-64E7-FD1066683DFC"
    ) .chezmoi.hostname -}}
mac_address: {{ $deskAddress | default "AA:AA:AA:AA:AA:AA" }}
positions:
  bottom: 0.62
  sit: 0.75
  stand: 1.1427
